s.e:
For time ſhall with his ready pencil ſtand;
Retouch your figures with his ripening hand;
Mellow your colors, and imbrown the teint;
Add every grace, which time…

[…] let them cast it [my soul] downe
Where refluent Oceanus doth crowne
His curled head;

A river girds the city west and south,
The main north channel of a broad lagoon,
Regurging with the salt tides from the mouth;
